      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That crushing feeling of permanence is a heavy and valid grief to carry, but please remember that future impact is not proof of current identity. People who feel this way often project a permanent \"self\" onto a temporary situation, missing that their capacity to do things differently has always been there, even if it hasn't been acknowledged until now. You are not a walking disaster waiting to break others; you are a human being in pain who needs to survive until they can rebuild their self-image.",
